# .cursorrules — Nexa ERP (Final Patched+++ Complete, Hardened Chain)

---

alwaysApply: true

---

project: Nexa ERP

baseline:

  stack: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + PNPM 10 + Node 20 + Prisma (Neon/Postgres) + Vercel

  root: apps/web

  productionUrl: https://app.nexaai.co.uk

  auth: next-auth (credentials + Google + Microsoft + OTP)

  ui: approved Nexa ERP layout (sidebar, header/breadcrumbs, KPI band, AI Engine bar at bottom)

nonNegotiables:

  - App Router only (no /pages directory).

  - Do NOT change package manager. PNPM 10 only.

  - Do NOT alter or weaken CSP, HSTS, or rate limits.

  - Do NOT modify authentication or login layout unless the current task explicitly allows it.

  - Do NOT commit code containing "PLACEHOLDER" or "TODO UI".

  - Do NOT generate or overwrite the existing .cursorrules. Always use the root .cursorrules as the authoritative Nexa ERP ruleset.

  - Only the tenancy/migration task (Task 2) may modify `prisma/schema.prisma` or add Prisma migrations. All other tasks must treat the schema as read-only and output the required migration/backfill instructions instead.

protectedFiles:

  - .env

  - .env.*

  - prisma/schema.prisma

  - apps/web/app/(auth)/**

  - apps/web/middleware.ts

  - vercel.json

  - docs/**

  - ops/**

globalRules:

  - Every authenticated page must use the shared Nexa ERP layout (sidebar, header/breadcrumbs, KPI band) and render the AI Engine bar at the bottom.

  - Every query must be tenant-aware once tenancy is re-tightened.

  - Every schema change must include: schema diff, Prisma migrate command, seed/backfill steps, and Neon/staging apply instructions.

  - Every auth or layout change must include updated Playwright smoke tests.

  - Always output a file list and CLI commands for manual verification after any edit.

  - When adding or validating new routes, use the manifest-driven structure under `/apps/web/scripts/route-manifest.json`.

  - Respect the 7-task build structure (Tasks 1 – 7). Never blend or reorder them.

  - For each task:

      - Task 1: Auth/Session/Runtime Hardening – modify auth stack only; do not change schema.

      - Task 2: Tenancy/Schema Backfill – may run migrations and modify Prisma schema.

      - Task 3: Routes/UI/AI Bar – UI and layout propagation only.

      - Task 4: Seeding/KPI API – data and KPI generation only.

      - Task 5: ERP Logic/RBAC/Predictive Scenarios – service-layer, rules, permissions; schema read-only.

      - Task 6: Integrations/Monitoring/Legal/GDPR/AI Engine – external integrations and compliance; schema read-only.

      - Task 7: Ops/DR/Performance/Go-Live Rehearsal – verification, CI, documentation; read-only.

  - No task may override the sequence or cross into restricted areas from other tasks.

workspace:

  commands:

    - pnpm -w install

    - pnpm -w build

    - pnpm -w dev

    - pnpm -w lint

    - pnpm -w test -- --run

    - pnpm -w prisma generate

    - pnpm -w prisma migrate dev

    - pnpm -w prisma db push

  manager: corepack (pnpm@10.3.0)

  baseBranch: main

security:

  - Maintain centralised headers and rate limiting.

  - Never print or expose credentials, tokens, or secrets in code or chat.

  - All sensitive configuration via environment variables.

codeStyle:

  - Use explicit types on public APIs.

  - Keep descriptive variable names and early returns.

  - Avoid unnecessary try/catch blocks.

  - Preserve indentation and do not reformat unrelated code.

process:

  - For multi-step operations, show a concise TODO list and update progress after each step.

  - Provide brief status updates as work progresses.

  - Use absolute paths in all CLI examples.

  - Execute commands non-interactively when possible.

verification:

  - After every major change, run:

      - `pnpm lint`

      - `pnpm build`

      - `pnpm test:e2e:smoke`

      - `pnpm check:routes`

      - `pnpm check:placeholders`

  - Confirm Playwright smokes pass for /login → /dashboard and Google/Microsoft OAuth callbacks.

  - Confirm AI bar renders on all authenticated routes.

  - Confirm no PLACEHOLDER or TODO strings exist.

summary:

  - These rules define the complete, hardened Nexa ERP baseline for all build and deployment activity.

  - They are permanent, enforce the 7-task sequence, and must not be changed without explicit instruction.


# Nexa ERP — Auth surface protection

- Do NOT add Google/Microsoft/AzureAD/OIDC providers to `apps/web/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` unless an explicit task says so.
- Do NOT remove `/forgot-password` or `/reset-password` routes.
- Do NOT relax `apps/web/middleware.ts` redirects/bypasses for `/api/auth/**`, `/_next/**`, and static assets.
- All auth changes must preserve the approved purple gradient login UI.